A||||7||FieroPerformance||Headlight Kits from Fiero Store?||||1||
Z||000000||FieroPerformance||04-27-2001||09:00 PM||||I was wondering if anyone has purchased the headlamp kits that the fierostore sells. I bought 2 cool blue headlights from Pep Boys expecting a blueish tint and was disapointed. Do the blue ion headlights the fiero store sells have a blue tint to them? (any pictures?)<P>Thanks,<BR>-Charlie<BR>------<BR>jackalrr@hotmail.com <A HREF="http://www.fieroperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroperformance.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierofreek2001||04-27-2001||10:45 PM||||i bought the blue kit from fiero store, and i love it, i get a lot of comments... and its actually a very good deal too, some modern cars now have to pay like 300$ for the same effect.... i just ordered the foglights a few days ago, and am installing them this weekend  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>sorry no pics.. but believe me.. there pretty damn blue!<BR>steve||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||04-27-2001||10:54 PM||||I had some of those blue tint bulbs in my Civic and they were really a headache- I mean a real headache! Night driving for long distances was aweful and now the bulbs are in the trash and the old standards are back in.||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT GT 87||04-27-2001||11:07 PM||||I went with the bright white ones from the Fiero Store.  The bulbs were not bright enough so I bought high powered ones frome The Car Botique , Bulbs alone were 85$  but more than twice as bright. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||04-28-2001||01:32 AM||||Yeah, The Fiero store's do have a good blue-ish tint to them. I think what you have in mind is the effect of HID lights, which are blue. Those suckers run about $700 to put on the fiero. I am still going to do it sometime this year, but I ran outta money with the engine project.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Taijiguy||04-28-2001||07:29 AM||||JC Whitney sells a true HID conversaion kit, and yeah, it's several hundred bucks. Obviously, the tinted bulbs aren't going to be as good as the HID system, or no one would pay for them.<BR>HID lights don't use a filament. They are actually an arc, like a welding arc. That's why they're so expensive and BRIGHT.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Alex2004||04-28-2001||02:23 PM||||Don't buy blue bulb's from wal-mart! i bought low & high beam blue bulb's for mom's Jag and you can hardly tell the difference.  It doesn't even look blue, it's basically just a bright white.  <B>Some</B> places that sell audio & tint windows sell blue bulbs.  They are around $30 a bulb but they are actually blue & still bright.  So you could check places like that.<P>Alex||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroPerformance||04-28-2001||09:14 PM||||They sound like they are worth a try. I really, really want the blue look.<P>Thanks,<BR>-Charlie||||reg||1
